-- ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Title: PIC32MX270F256B @sim_validate — tail-transfer keeps code + values
-- Author: Matthew Schinkel, Copyright (c) 2026 all rights reserved.
-- Compiler: JALv2
--
-- Description:
--    Port of **18f4620_compiler_regression_tail_return.jal** to PIC32
--    (@sim_validate / QEMU). Guards **`cmd_opt_tail_return`** /
--    **`cmd_opt_branch`**: on MIPS the deleted tail GOTO truncated the
--    caller before its epilogue → stale-`$ra` infinite loop
--    (****); the same body also
--    checks the deleted side effects / wrong return values.
--    Uses the shared body **`tests/_regression_tail_return_body.jal`**
--    via the classic helpers (`regression_pic32`), so the checks are
--    identical across all four suite architectures.
--
-- Notes:
--    ./bin/jalv3-x86-64 -s 'lib;tests' tests/pic32/32mx270f256b_tail_return_regression.jal
--
-- @sim_validate begin
-- duration_s: 0.5
-- machine: pic32mx7-explorer16
-- expect byte v__check_step 6
-- @sim_validate end
--
-- ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

include regression_32mx270f256b_device
include regression_pic32

-- `led` / `led_pin` come from the device prelude (RAM-backed LED stub);
-- `_usec_delay` from the device library. Classic-equivalent body below.

include _regression_tail_return_body
